 Its swinging through air,
 and air currents,
 eddies,
 and of course,
 the trailing turbulent wake alter the flow.
 Modeling this becomes a practical impossibility.
 And its worse:
 it might even be hit by an ultra–high energy cosmic ray,
 coming from some distant supernova.
 The entanglement of the actual physical system is absurd.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
When an actual,
 physical double pendulum has actually swung about,
 what,
 exactly,
 has ingressed?
 The differential equation describing an idealized double pendulum has this structure,
 a symplectic manifold with particle trajectories on it,
 and a countable number of bifurcation points embedded into it:
 saddle points strewn all through it,
 organizable into an infinite binary tree.
 But what ingresses is not one of these perfect,
 point–like trajectories,
 but some bundle.
 A bundle,
 if for no other reason that we have to consider the thermodynamic canonical ensemble of the grease in the bearings,
 and the air through which it swings.
 An uncountable number of idealized trajectories cut through this bundle,
 entering and existing as dampening and friction remove energy from the system.
 So,
 again,
 what's ingressing?
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
There are two issues here.
 One is that if a distant supernova can emit a cosmic ray that disturbs the pendulum motion,
 the problem becomes unbounded:
 potentially anything in the universe can affect the motion.
 So that is one issue.
 The second issue is that the underlying theory is quantum.
 So,
 imagine if we could,
 the ability to simulate the entire universe,
 with the double–pendulum in it,
 so that every last atom and photon is accounted for.
 Even then,
 the movement can only be approximately classical.
 That is,
 here–and–now is inherently quantum–mechanical;
 the set of possible futures are always those that are a few hbar away from the (collapsing) present.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
And what of panpsychism,
 of hylozoism?
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Lets super–ultra–duper simplify the system.
 Imagine a de Sitter universe,
 entirely empty but for this pendulum.
 Or perhaps just a flat Newtonin universe.
 Imagine the double pendulum made of two elemental links.
 Perfect links,
 not made of atoms,
 but connected,
 having mass.
 Described by quantum mechanics.
\end_layout

